{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two dice appear to be normal dice with their faces numbered from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but each die is weighted so that the probability of rolling the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is directly proportional to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. The probability of rolling a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with this pair of dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is easier to think of the dice as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sided dice with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sixes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fives, etc.  Then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47ad5c1e8a5ebf5f2c75e4198d926fc5def5b006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21^2=441$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> possible rolls. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/59299c5f2feee7ad487c231c304ff30f59568047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot(1\\cdot 6+2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 4)=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" /> rolls that will result in a seven.  The odds are therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9011f3ff0a4fa06c2cdc938526d618228d14bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{56}{441}=\\frac{8}{63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359026a1e115a5ea0995922f74528389ed4eb011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+63=\\boxed{071}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>See also <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the probability of rolling any number is 1, and the problem tells us the dice are unfair, we can assign probabilities to the individual faces. The probability of rolling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c8b38e55642a33c3e1a256a74b9bdd4ea743a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"34\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d97724c16518934c53b127b318c585e00531bf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21=\\frac{6 \\cdot 7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />\nNext, we notice that 7 can be rolled by getting individual results of 1 and 6, 2 and 5, or 3 and 4 on the separate dice. \nThe probability that 7 is rolled is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f893bb05cef52b15d8dc0e01ad64a62935e14bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(\\frac{1}{21} \\cdot \\frac{6}{21}+\\frac{2}{21} \\cdot \\frac{5}{21} + \\frac{3}{21} \\cdot \\frac{4}{21})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"38\" /> which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9011f3ff0a4fa06c2cdc938526d618228d14bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{56}{441}=\\frac{8}{63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />.  Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359026a1e115a5ea0995922f74528389ed4eb011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+63=\\boxed{071}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n~PEKKA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the probability of rolling a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b85cf5e2348b02fc8962cd11cc595bc37bcee6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, the probability of rolling a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c3712ba822a3cc0c57dbaf005b4cfbf8979b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> the probability of rolling a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a94daf5dd53bfc4620c82a53454c5f2029898a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> and so on, we can make a chart of probabilities and add them together. Note that we only need the probabilities of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the rest is symmetry and the others are irrelevant. \n</p><p>We have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c5d78ef42ac8f40bdd06a8842577f441194601c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{21} \\cdot \\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159e17aaff6f9c873520a94e79161bb75ee1b34d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{21} \\cdot \\frac{5}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e6745aa3e81236f224e4cafc6122ec8b16e2c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{7} \\cdot \\frac{4}{21})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e15e0ab33fa7a066ba28e8a76ede5996c5082a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot (\\frac{2}{147} + \\frac{10}{441} + \\frac{4}{147})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/343765f62d03a3138f2bc3693ccef9e3194c172d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{4}{63} = \\frac{8}{63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692eae0df2ee50f57f83258f20c284d8f0979cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8fd978f90e625f8a23042ec6a33efd5f3a910e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{071}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145754\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 302/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8047/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.408      1 -total\n 59.01%    7.322      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.15%    4.858      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14849:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017145754 and revision id 163669. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}